  "body": {
    "id": "thm:complexity-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For \\(1\\le H_n\\le\\lfloor n^{1/8}\\rfloor\\), there exist constants \\(0<c<C<\\infty\\), depending only on the class radii, such that uniformly over \\(\\mathbb P\\in\\mathcal C_n\\), \\(\\kappa_{\\mathrm{rec},n}\\le C\\) and \\(c(1+\\rho_n)\\le\\kappa_{\\mathrm{dir},n}\\le C(1+\\rho_n)\\). Moreover, \\(c\\sqrt{\\nu_{\\min,n}\\log(2H_n)}\\le\\rho_n\\le C\\sqrt{\\nu_{\\max,n}\\log(2H_n)}\\). Hence direct complexity is bounded if and only if \\(\\rho_n=O(1)\\). If all shares vanish, direct complexity is bounded; if \\(\\nu_{\\min,n}>0\\) and \\(\\nu_{\\max,n}\\le K\\nu_{\\min,n}\\) uniformly, then \\(\\kappa_{\\mathrm{dir},n}\\asymp1+\\sqrt{\\nu_{\\min,n}\\log(2H_n)}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n",
      "\\mathcal C_n",
      "\\kappa_{m,n}",
      "\\nu_{n,\\ell}",
      "\\nu_{\\min,n}",
      "\\nu_{\\max,n}",
